(in-package :web-skeleton-tests)

;;; ===========================================================================
;;; ECDSA P-256 verification corpus
;;;
;;; Entries are (NAME EXPECTED DIGEST SIGNATURE X Y), the last four in hex: a
;;; 32-byte digest, the 64-byte r || s, and the public key's two 32-byte
;;; coordinates. EXPECTED is T for a signature that verifies and NIL for one
;;; that must not.
;;;
;;; Every verdict is OpenSSL's, and any entry can be put to it again: write
;;; the digest to dig.bin, r and s as a DER ECDSA-Sig-Value to sig.der, the
;;; key as a SubjectPublicKeyInfo to pub.der, and run
;;;
;;;   openssl pkeyutl -verify -pubin -keyform DER -inkey pub.der \
;;;                   -in dig.bin -sigfile sig.der
;;;
;;; With web-skeleton-tls loaded, TEST-ECDSA-CORPUS asks libssl about every
;;; entry as well, so each run with TLS checks the corpus against OpenSSL.
;;;
;;; Three kinds of entry:
;;;
;;;   openssl key K digest D   keys made and digests signed by OpenSSL, each
;;;                            with its twin (r, n - s), which RFC 7518 also
;;;                            accepts: one of the two is high-S.
;;;   key K digest D: ...      one of those with one thing changed: a digest
;;;                            bit, an r or s bit, r and s swapped, another
;;;                            key, the negated key, or r or s at 0, 1,
;;;                            n - 1, n and 2^256 - 1.
;;;   crafted: ...             signatures computed from a known private key,
;;;                            for what a random signature never reaches:
;;;                            s = 1 and n - 1; u1 = 0 and 1; u2 = 1; a
;;;                            digest at or above n; the halves of
;;;                            u1 G + u2 Q equal, so the sum doubles, or
;;;                            opposite, so it is the point at infinity; and
;;;                            the public keys G, -G and 2G, under which
;;;                            G + Q is 2G, infinity and 3G.
;;; ===========================================================================

